WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:11.830
35. Hold on to your pocket money. One day you'll need to learn how to save money, even

2
00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:19.110
if you don't have anything to save for right now. Get used to saving and budgeting now.

3
00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:23.970
Then you'll have money when you do want something expensive and you'll be practicing for your

4
00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:31.290
future. Tip 1. Be clear about how much money you have coming in. Do you get your allowance

5
00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:37.990
weekly or monthly? Do you earn any other money? Total your money for the period you want to

6
00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:47.750
budget for. Tip 2. Separate needs from wants. You need money for transportation. You want to have

7
00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:55.290
money left over for snacks and games. Then decide which of your wants should get priority and which

8
00:00:55.290 --> 00:01:03.590
ones you can let go. Tip 3. Make a budget. Once you know how much money you will have in a period

9
00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:10.270
of time, you can decide how to spend it. Separate the money for your needs and don't touch it for

10
00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:18.230
anything else. Then add up how much your wants will cost. See if you can make your needs and wants add

11
00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:28.090
up to 90% or less of your total allowance. Tip 4. Put your savings, the 10% or more that you

12
00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:34.650
aren't spending each month, far away. Put them in a bank or somewhere that you can't reach easily.

13
00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:43.090
You'll be less tempted to use them that way. Tip 5. Write your expenses down, at least until you

14
00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:49.550
can get used to what they are. This way, you'll know where your money is going and what you need

15
00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:59.390
to do to hold on to it longer. Tip 6. Put a little bit away every day. Even if it's just change, get

16
00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:05.630
used to having something left over. You'll be surprised at how much change adds up over months.
